  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Los doce animales",
    "@en": "The 12 animals"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "En Vietnam se usa el calendario solar (**dương lịch**) para la vida diaria y el lunar (**âm lịch**) para fiestas tradicionales. El ciclo zodiacal lunar asigna un animal a cada año y se repite cada 12 años.",
     "@en": "In Vietnam, the solar calendar (**dương lịch**) is used for daily life and lunar (**âm lịch**) for traditional parties. The lunar zodiacal cycle assigns one animal to each year and is repeated every 12 years."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Es muy habitual que te pregunten: **Anh tuổi con gì?** = ¿De qué animal eres? Respuesta: **Tôi tuổi con rồng.** = Soy dragón.",
     "@en": "It's very common to be asked: **Anh tuổi con gì?** = What animal are you from? Answer: **Tôi tuổi con rồng.** = I am a dragon."
    },
    {
     "@es": "En el zodiaco vietnamita, el cuarto animal es el **gato (mèo)**; en otros zodiacos de la región puede aparecer el conejo.",
     "@en": "In the Vietnamese zodiac, the fourth animal is the **gato (mèo)**; in other zodiacs in the region the rabbit may appear."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Los nombres tradicionales sino-vietnamitas (Tý, Sửu, Dần…) aparecen en calendarios y expresiones: **Tôi tuổi Thìn** = Soy del año del dragón.",
     "@en": "The traditional Sino-Vietnamese names (Tý, Sửu, Dần) appear in calendars and expressions: **Tôi tuổi Thìn** = I'm from the dragon year."
    },
    {
     "@es": "El año nuevo lunar es el **Tết Nguyên Đán** (o simplemente Tết). Antes se celebraba con petardos (**pháo**).",
     "@en": "The lunar new year is the **Tết Nguyên Đán** (or simply Tết). It used to be celebrated with firecrackers (**pháo**)."
    }
   ]
  },
